 | stoppingThreshold                 | float      | 0.1 (m/s)         | Maximum velocity to start charging                      |
 
+The `Energy` model accepts either recuperation limit independently. It represents the mechanical braking work in each time step as a constant braking force and assumes the speed changes linearly during the step.
+With ideal gearing, `maximumRecuperationTorque` limits the regenerative force at the wheels to the shaft torque times `gearRatio` divided by `wheelRadius`.
+If this force times the vehicle speed exceeds `maximumRecuperationPower`, the motor accepts only the configured power for that portion of the step.
+Friction brakes dissipate the excess braking energy.
+Recuperation efficiency and auxiliary consumption apply after the mechanical limits. A zero value for either limit disables recuperation.
+
 !!! note
     Before SUMO 1.20.0 the `rotatingMass` was called `internalMomentOfInertia` but it has been renamed to make clear
     that it is a mass and not a moment of inertia. The old parameter is considered deprecated.
